  "summary": "The tomb of Cyrus at Pasargadae is a small stone chamber on a plinth of six receding tiers, about 11 m tall, linked to the death of Cyrus the Great around 530 BCE. Alexander the Great ordered restorations of the tomb in January 324 BCE. It forms part of the UNESCO-listed Pasargadae.",
